<div class="empty-state">
  <h1>📊 Metrics Dashboard</h1>
  <p>Metrics database not yet available.</p>

  <div class="info-box">
    <h2>🚀 Quick Start:</h2>
    <p>To see metrics, you need to run an agent session that will generate events and populate <code>.boukensha/events.db</code>.</p>

    <h3>Steps:</h3>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Run a session:</strong>
        <pre style="background: #2a2a2a; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto;">
cd week2_capable
python -m boukensha.run --session demo_run
        </pre>
      </li>
      <li><strong>Or run with MUD integration:</strong>
        <pre style="background: #2a2a2a; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto;">
python -m boukensha.run --config config.yaml --session live_run
        </pre>
      </li>
      <li><strong>Refresh this page</strong> to see live metrics populate</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>📈 What Metrics Will Show:</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Token Economy</strong> — breakdown by schema, history, results, output</li>
      <li><strong>Schema Overhead (M4)</strong> — tool gating effectiveness</li>
      <li><strong>Cache Effectiveness (M8)</strong> — prompt cache hit rate and cost savings</li>
      <li><strong>M9 Compression</strong> — repeat-room savings and frontier queries
        <ul>
          <li>Compression events logged as <code>phase: "tokens.compressed"</code></li>
          <li>Contains: before_tokens, after_tokens, saved, visit_count, room_id</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li><strong>Context Compaction (M3)</strong> — compaction events and message drops</li>
      <li><strong>Tool Usage</strong> — success rates by tool</li>
      <li><strong>Iteration Analysis</strong> — tokens per turn, context pressure</li>
      <li><strong>Exploration Progress</strong> — rooms discovered, confidence levels</li>
      <li><strong>Permissions & Audit (M5)</strong> — allow/deny/ask decisions</li>
      <li><strong>Recommendations</strong> — automated optimization suggestions</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Sample metrics shown:</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Token Economy</strong> — breakdown by schema, history, results</li>
      <li><strong>Schema Overhead</strong> — M4 tool gating effectiveness</li>
      <li><strong>Caching</strong> — M8 prompt cache hit rate and savings</li>
      <li><strong>M9 Compression</strong> — repeat-room savings and frontier queries</li>
      <li><strong>Iteration Analysis</strong> — context pressure and compaction</li>
      <li><strong>Exploration Progress</strong> — rooms discovered, confidence levels</li>
      <li><strong>Tool Usage</strong> — success rates by tool</li>
      <li><strong>Recommendations</strong> — optimizations suggested</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

